    706:| Connes-Consani-Moscovici spectral-triple operator (arXiv:2511.22755) as polylog architecture for pi(x) (Chain A step 4 / FOCUS-1 / E3.1) | FAIL | E | Numerical proxy: rank-one self-adjoint perturbation V = c\|v><v\| of discretized scaling operator D = -i d/du on L^2([-L,L]), L = log(lambda), x_cutoff = 10^4, N=1200 Fourier modes; v built from von-Mangoldt-weighted prime-power delta-comb in log space (best variant). Sweep B in {1..9} primes ({2}, {2,3}, ..., {2..23}); coupling tuned at B=6. Median matched-error[:50] flat at 0.13-0.20 across all B (no monotonic decrease in B); K_accurate(<0.5) saturates at 50/50 by comb-density artefact (also true for B=0 control); under monotone test (mu_K vs gamma_K), K_accurate=0 for all B. Proxy does NOT reproduce CCM's published 10^{-55} accuracy on err[1] (off by ~53 orders), but scaling-law conclusion is independent of kernel choice. Three independent arguments close polylog claim: (i) rank-one perturbation has B parameters; Cauchy interlacing limits eigenvalue placement to ~B substantial shifts; (ii) diagonalization of N x N truncation costs O(N^3) = O(K^3) for K eigenvalues — worse than O(x^{1/2+eps}) summation; (iii) CCM's published B=6 -> K=50 with err range 10^{-55..-3} implies geometric per-zero error growth ~11.3x, yielding K_accurate(B=6) ~ 53 even at face value, with NO multi-B data point in the literature establishing super-linear scaling. Even granting most-generous linear K_accurate(B)=B, reaching K=10^50 zeros for p(10^100) requires B ~ 10^50 primes, identical to existing O(sqrt(x)) zero-summation barrier. Closes E3.1's elevated edge value to baseline analytic equivalence. See experiments/analytic/connes_operator/. | 53 |
